Exercise
Let’s make use of what we have learned in the previous section to replicate the previous pregnancy section in Table 1
Try out this exercise below. Ensure that

The labels are set correctly,
Statistics are displayed as counts (as integers) and percentages (in one decimal place).
p values are displayed in two decimal places.



















NoteHint





Take a look at how age race and education summary table is created and copy its parameters to the previous pregnancy table.











TipFully worked solution:







opt_previous_preg_data |&gt;
  gtsummary::tbl_summary(
    include = c(
      "Prev.preg",
      "previous_live_preterm_birth",
      "Spont.ab", "Induced.ab", "Any.stillbirth"
    ),
    by = "Group",
    missing = "no",
    label = list(
      "Prev.preg" ~ "Any pregancy",
      "previous_live_preterm_birth" ~ "Live preterm birth",
      "Spont.ab" ~ "Spontaneous abortion",
      "Induced.ab" ~ "Induced abortion",
      "Any.stillbirth" ~ "Stillbirth"
    ),
    statistic = list(
      gtsummary::all_categorical() ~ "{n} ({p})"
    ),
    digits = list(
      gtsummary::all_categorical() ~ c(0, 1)
    )
  ) |&gt; 
  gtsummary::add_variable_group_header(
    header = "Previous pregnancies - no. (%)",
    variables = c(
      "Prev.preg",
      "previous_live_preterm_birth",
      "Spont.ab", "Induced.ab", "Any.stillbirth"
    )
  )|&gt; 
  gtsummary::add_p(
    pvalue_fun = gtsummary::label_style_pvalue(digits = 2)
  ) |&gt; 
  gtsummary::remove_footnote_header()
