Exercise (Remove p value from Total)
Here is live_birth and its corresponding table_body that we have so far.

current live birthtable_body


Click on the different tabs.























Use gtsummary::modify_table_body to remove the p value from the Total.


















NoteHint





Ensure the dplyr::case_when function is something like this
dplyr::case_when(
  .data[["variable"]] == "Have_Live_Birth" ~ NA,
  .default = .data[["p.value"]]
)











TipFully worked solution:







live_birth |&gt;
  gtsummary::modify_table_body(
    ~ .x |&gt; 
      dplyr::mutate(
        `p.value` = dplyr::case_when(
          .data[["variable"]] == "Have_Live_Birth" ~ NA,
          .default = .data[["p.value"]]
        )
      )
  )
live_birth |&gt;
